=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_4a7f — Weekday Evening: Yuki's Kitchen, 18 to 22

Marco is at work (out from ~13:40 to ~22:00) on weekday evenings, so Yuki runs the kitchen alone. The patrol passes at 18:00, 20:00, and 22:00 trace a clear cooking-then-cleanup arc: at 18:00 the cutting board is on the counter and the knife is still in the drawer (prep is beginning); by 20:00 the board and knife are in the sink (being washed), the pan and spatula are on the counter (active cooking), and Yuki's plate, glass, water bottle, and the serving dish are all at the kitchen table (she is eating); by 22:00 everything is put away—board back on the counter, knife in the cupboard, pan in the pantry, dishes in the cupboard, glass in the cupboard, water bottle back in the dish rack. Yuki was seen in the kitchen at 20:00, confirming she is the one cooking and eating. The pot briefly appears in the drawer at 20:00 (perhaps a lid or a small pot set aside while the main pan is in use).

This document sets itself apart by placing the in-use cooking window at 18:30–21:00 (the gap between the 18:00 and 20:00 passes is when prep transitions to active cooking; the 20:00 pass catches the peak) and the meal window at 19:30–21:00 (plates and glasses at the table at 20:00, gone by 22:00). It predicts that the cutting board and knife will be in the sink, not the counter or drawer, during the 19:00–21:00 window, and that the pan will be on the counter (not in the cupboard) during 19:00–21:30.

Refutation: if a look at 19:00–21:00 finds the cutting board still on the counter (not yet washed) or the pan still in the cupboard (not yet in use), the cooking window is wrong. If plates are at the table at 22:00, the meal runs later than predicted.

