=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_8c2e — Yuki's Keys: Short Errand, Home by Five

The only keys in this household are keys_yuki (Yuki is retired; Marco does not appear to carry a separate tracked set). The patrol data shows keys_yuki most often at entry_table_e1 (1/1 sighted days, 3 sightings). The claim in p_a1b2 that the keys are OUT_OF_HOUSE for the entire 14:00–22:00 window has gone against twice (keys sighted in the house during that span) while also earning three weak-for hits (looks at entry_table_e1 finding nothing). The most parsimonious reading: Yuki takes her keys for a mid-afternoon errand (roughly 14:30–15:30, consistent with the "afternoon errands" in her profile) and is back home by 16:00, keys returned to the entry table. The rest of the evening (16:00–22:00) she is in the house—cooking, guitar, TV—so the keys sit on the entry table.

This document differs from p_a1b2 by narrowing the out-of-house window to 14:30–15:30 instead of 14:00–22:00, and from p_c9d4 (which puts Yuki out 13:00–17:30) by keeping her home from 15:30 onward. It predicts the keys will be at the entry table at 17:00, 19:00, and 21:00 on weekdays.

Refutation: if the keys are found out of the house (or in Yuki's hand) after 16:00 on a weekday, the short-errand model is wrong. If the keys are missing from the entry table at 14:00 (before the predicted errand start), the window is earlier.

